# syncto example targets file
#
# Copy to ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/syncto/targets, or just use
# `syncto --add <name> <path> [k=v,...]` and let syncto write it for you.
# Nothing in this repo is read at runtime — real config lives outside it.
#
# Format — TSV: name<TAB>path<TAB>options
#
#   - Fields are tab-separated. Exactly one target per line.
#   - `path` MUST have $HOME written literally as `~` (not expanded), so the same
#     file works unmodified across machines and usernames. syncto expands it at
#     read time, and writes it back in `~` form when you use --add.
#   - `options` is a comma-separated list of key=value pairs. Every key is
#     optional; omitted keys fall back to the defaults in `config`.
#
# Recognized option keys:
#   interval=<seconds>          how often the daemon/scheduler syncs this target
#   watch=on|off                also sync on file-change, not just on schedule
#   debounce=<seconds>          quiet period a watcher waits before syncing (default 2)
#   mode=sync|push|pull         sync = pull+push (default), push/pull = one-way only
#   branch=<name>               override the global default branch
#   remote=<name>               override the global default remote
#   prefix=<commit msg prefix>  e.g. "notes (laptop)" -> "notes (laptop): file.md"
#   guard=<shell cmd>           must exit 0 or this pass is skipped for this target
#   stale=<seconds>|off         alert when no sync has succeeded for this long
#                               (default: 12x interval, at least 600s)
#   notify=<shell cmd>          run on unresolvable conflict (exit 2) or staleness
#   peer=<shell cmd>            run after a successful commit+push, best-effort
#
# A comma inside a value must be escaped as \, — see docs/design.md.
#
# Two examples: a notes repo synced two-way with a guard and a conflict notifier,
# and a dotfiles repo that pokes another machine to pull right after a push.

notes	~/notes	interval=120,watch=on,prefix=notes (laptop),guard=test $(find ~/notes -maxdepth 1 -name '*.partial' | wc -l) -eq 0,notify=notify-send "syncto conflict" "notes needs a human"
dotfiles	~/dotfiles	interval=300,mode=sync,branch=main,remote=origin,prefix=dotfiles,peer=ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o BatchMode=yes example-host "systemctl --user start syncto.service"
